{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:11318265b83212da","name":"Dathomiri Witch Talent Tree","source":{"id":"source:reference-11318265b83212da","title":"Dathomiri Witch Talent Tree","revision":18094,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T19:34:48Z","sha256":"57161175957c04b709bf8866e52ebc7dc8d17c8832086712d732af88ee532553","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18094","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Dathomiri%20Witch%20Talent%20Tree&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-11318265b83212da","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Force-using witches of the planet ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dathomir"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dathomir?action=edit&redlink=1"}," are primitive yet powerful beings. They use ancient training handed down for generations as the basis of their powers. Only Force-users that are part of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Witches of Dathomir"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Witches_of_Dathomir","referenceId":"reference:967d8c890fd22a13"}," may select ",{"tag":"a","children":["Talents"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Talents","referenceId":"reference:e8871b70ebfa07d9"}," from this tree.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Core Talents"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Adept Spellcaster"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["You may use any ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Power"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Power"}," that normally requires a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Move Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Move_Action"},", or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Standard Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Standard_Action"}," as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Full-Round Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Full-Round_Action"}," instead. If you choose to do so, you may reroll your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use the Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_the_Force","referenceId":"reference:74883d1dd46b87fe"}," check to activate that power, but you must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Dathomiri Charm Beast"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["You may use a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use the Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_the_Force","referenceId":"reference:74883d1dd46b87fe"}," check in place of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Persuasion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Persuasion","referenceId":"reference:196fbdc5f1823320"}," check when attempting to change the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Attitude"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Attitude"}," of an undomesticated creature with an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intelligence"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intelligence"}," of 2 or less. Additionally, you do not take the normal -5 penalty on the check if the creature can't speak or understand your language. This Talent is identical to the ",{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Beastwarden Charm Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beastwarden_Charm_Beast"}]}," Talent, and both are considered to be the same for the purposes of satisfying prerequisites.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Dathomiri Command Beast"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Prerequisite:"]}," ",{"tag":"b","children":["Dathomiri Charm Beast"]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Whenever you manage to shift the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Attitude"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Attitude"}," of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," to Indifferent or Friendly, you may treat that creature as a domesticated animal- but for you only (it remains undomesticated in its response to other creatures). Additionally, you may use this ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," as a mount, as per the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ride"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ride","referenceId":"reference:439efdc566bb419f"}," skill, provided that it is at least one size category larger than you and has a comfortable place for you to sit.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Flight"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Prerequisite:"]}," ",{"tag":"b","children":["Adept Spellcaster"]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["As a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"},", you can spend a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Point"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Point"}," to fly. You gain a Fly Speed equal to your base ",{"tag":"a","children":["Speed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Speed","referenceId":"reference:c372fee9b4566b85"},", and you can ascend at half speed or descend at double speed. The ",{"tag":"b","children":["Flight"]}," lasts until the start of your next turn; if you're still airborne at that time, you fall.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
